   "t": "html",
   "html": "<div class=\"desc\"><p>The UdsTransportProtocolMgr class manages the interaction between the Diagnostic Server instance(s) and various UDS Transport Protocols (e.g., DoIP<a class=\"bibref\" href=\"https://www.iso.org/standard/74785.html\" title=\"ISO 13400-2:2019 – Road vehicles – Diagnostic communication over Internet Protocol (DoIP) – Part 2: Network and transport layer requirements and services (Edition 2, Release 2019-12)\">[2]</a>, CAN<a class=\"bibref\" href=\"#fn-head-21\" title=\"ISO 15765-2 – Road vehicles – Diagnostics on Controller Area Networks (CAN) – Part2: Network layer services\">[21]</a>). It provides a standard, extensible API for handling transport-specific message reception and optional early payload access.</p><p class=\"fnote\">Literaturverzeichnis SWS Diagnostics: <span id=\"fn-head-2\">[2] ISO 13400-2:2019 – Road vehicles – Diagnostic communication over Internet Protocol (DoIP) – Part 2: Network and transport layer requirements and services (Edition 2, Release 2019-12) – <a href=\"https://www.iso.org/standard/74785.html\">www.iso.org</a></span> <br><span id=\"fn-head-21\">[21] ISO 15765-2 – Road vehicles – Diagnostics on Controller Area Networks (CAN) – Part2: Network layer services</span></p></div>",
   "tail": "\n"
  },
